# {{DISPLAY}}

One paragraph: what the agent actually does. No marketing.

## Workflow

1. Decide whether this skill applies. If not, stop.
2. Do the default path with the bundled script (if any).
3. Return concrete artifacts (paths, not dumps).

Default command (forward slashes; `<skill-dir>` is this folder):

```bash
python3 "<skill-dir>/scripts/example.py" path/to/input
```

If `python3` is missing, use `py -3` with the same arguments.

## Quality gate

- Output matches what the user asked for.
- No secrets in files or logs.
- Failures tell the agent what to fix.

Read [references/notes.md](references/notes.md) only when the default path is not enough.
